module test.claim.product.p4261_photograph_witness

// WHAT THIS WITNESS HOLDS. product.electrical.photograph says a claim about the board can cite the frame
// it was read from, by the SHA-256 of that frame's bytes, and product.p4261.e1_photographs holds the 201
// records the 2026-11-03 E1 atlas produced: 192 frames somebody photographed and 9 views we drew. The claim worth defending is one sentence: A BOARD ROW IS
// CHECKABLE AGAINST AN IMAGE ONLY IF THE STORE HOLDS THE BYTES IT NAMES. Everything below attacks the
// ways that sentence gets faked -- a citation that resolves to nothing and still reads as evidence, a
// digest somebody guessed, a file name used as an identity, an image we drew used to corroborate the
// readings it was drawn from, a pixel box quietly dropped, or a gap written so smoothly it looks like a
// receipt.
//
// IT RUNS LOCALLY, NOT IN CI. Public CI runs no witnesses, and the required `v2-bootstrap` job does not
// evaluate them (DESIGN, "What a green v2-bootstrap does not say"). Build the seed from a public worktree
// and run each name below:
//
//   cargo build --release -p v1-compiler --bin gunbc
//   GUNBC_MEMORY_BUDGET_BYTES=6442450944 ./target/release/gunbc run --claim-run \
//     --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 \
//     --entry dag/test/claim/product/p4261_photograph_witness.dag --function <name>
//
// (unset GUNBC_RESOLVED_GRAPH_CACHE_DIR and GUNBC_NATIVE_CACHE_ROOT first).

